{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "Lateralus and Aenima feel like natural next choices after 10.000 Days because I want more of Tool's heavy sound and intricate songs.",
    "The Downward Spiral's abrasive darkness and Christ Illusion's thrash intensity connect with the heavier music I explored through In Flames, Death Cult Armageddon, and Advance And Vanquish."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Wincing the Night Away feels too light for my current mood; being another rock album does not give it the weight I am looking for.",
    "Stadium Arcadium's funk-influenced sound is less compelling right now because I am drawn toward darker, heavier music."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My earlier interest in accessible rock seems to carry too much weight when my latest choices point more strongly toward Tool and heavier music.",
    "Aggression alone does not make an album a top choice for me: St. Anger fits that mood, but Tool's intricate songs are more appealing today."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My most recent choice, 10.000 Days, makes continuing with Tool especially appealing, beyond simply choosing another heavy album.",
    "An album can fit my taste without being something I would choose now: October Rust's atmosphere and Year Zero's industrial sound interest me, but I would prioritize Tool and try The Downward Spiral first."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations understand my interest in dark, heavy music, but some give too much weight to broad rock similarities and too little to my current pull toward Tool's intricate sound."
}"}
